        "original_id": "469291b0-4767-5cd3-a1c4-30a6287c3b41",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sila Region, Chad, Libya, Sudan, Central African Republic, Cameroon, Nigeria, Niger, Markounda, Tripoli\n- Organizations/Regions: Ouaddaï Region\n- Places/Buildings: Gurgi Mosque\n\nFacts:\n- Chad is bordered by Libya to the north, Sudan to the east, the Central African Republic to the south, Cameroon and Nigeria to the southwest, and Niger to the west.\n- In 2008, Sila Region was created in Chad from the departments of Sila and Djourf Al Ahmar, which had previously been part of Ouaddaï Region.\n- Markounda is a sub-prefecture that borders Chad.\n- Gurgi Mosque is a mosque in Tripoli, Libya.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
